 Record 866 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: XCO Library\nDescription: XCO XSLX: You can now style the fonts of a cell of an Excel worksheet.  For more information, see XCO Library.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-16\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n--- Record 867 ---\nComponent: Cloud Transport Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New feedback button is available in the title bar of SAP Cloud Transport Management\nDescription: Use the feedback button to share anonymous feedback about SAP Cloud Transport Management.See:   SAP Cloud Transport Management Home Screen  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Application Development and Integration\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-16\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: 2504b\n\n--- Record 868 ---\nComponent: Cloud Transport Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: SAP Cloud Transport Management service available on new data centers.\nDescription: SAP Cloud Transport Management service is now also available in the following regions:  Amazon Web Services in the US West (Oregon) region   Azure in the Canada Central (Toronto) region   See:   SAP Cloud Transport Management in SAP Discovery Center  Regions and API Endpoints Available for the Cloud Foundry Environment  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Application Development and Integration\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-16\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 869 ---\nComponent: Joule,SAP BTP Cockpit\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: UX Improvements to Joule in SAP BTP Cockpit\nDescription: Scenario flows and texts have been optimized for Joule interactions.  Joule in the cockpit now supports multiple attributes when selecting entities. For example, you can select a subaccount by entering the subaccount display name, subaccount ID, and/or subdomain name. Joule validates the name you enter and provides suggestions should it not recognize your entry.  Entities and attributes:  Cloud Foundry Space: ID name, space name  Global Account: subdomain, display name  User: email address  Role Collection: name  Region: region (technical name), display name  Subaccount: ID, display name, subdomain  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType\",1715\n465,\" subaccount display name, subaccount ID, and/or subdomain name. Joule validates the name you enter and provides suggestions should it not recognize your entry.  Entities and attributes:  Cloud Foundry Space: ID name, space name  Global Account: subdomain, display name  User: email address  Role Collection: name  Region: region (technical name), display name  Subaccount: ID, display name, subdomain  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-16\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 870 ---\nComponent: Multitarget Applications for Cloud Foundry\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Removal of SAP Java Buildpack 1\nDescription: SAP Java Buildpack 1 has been deprecated and will be removed from SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment on June 30, 2025. As a consequence, deployments of MTAs containing modules of type java, java.tomcat, and java.tomee might start to fail, as the buildpack used by default is SAP Java Buildpack 1.   To ensure compliance with this change, starting from the beginning of July, the MTA deployment will switch the default value for the buildpack parameter from sap_java_buildpack (SAP Java Buildpack 1) to sap_java_buildpack_jakarta (SAP Java Buildpack 2).  Action:  Plan and migrate your applications to SAP Java Buildpack 2 ahead of the scheduled change. In your deployment descriptors, you need to explicitly set one of the parameters buildpack or buildpacks of the java, java.tomcat, and java.tomee modules to sap_java_buildpack_jakarta. Note that this transition involves more than just configuration updates and may require code modifications.  See:  Migrate your Applications to SAP Java Buildpack 2  SAP Java Buildpack 2: Jakarta-Based, Fresh and New!  TomEE 10 has landed in SAP Java Buildpack 2!  \nAction: Required\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-15\nValid as Of: 2025-05-15\nVersion: Cloud\n\n\",1457\n610,\"--- Record 781 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: API Gateway module: Update to version 3.0.4\nDescription: This release contains the following improvements:  We've unified extensibility views for APIGateway and APIRule custom resources in Busola.  Now, the order of rules in the APIRule custom resource is important. Rules defined earlier in the list have a higher priority than those defined later. For more information, see Significance of Rule Path Order.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-22\nValid as Of: 2025-05-26\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 782 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pricing - Access with Multiple Multi-Valued Attributes\nDescription: An access sequence that includes an access with multiple multi-valued attributes, such as KOMP-VARCOND and KOMP-COCO_NUM, used to lead to an unexpected system error. This issue has been corrected.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-02\nValid as Of: 2025-05-26\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 783 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Google PubSub Adapter supports WIF(Workload Identity Federation) authentication and On-Premise Connectivity.\nDescription: A new version 1.1.0 of Google PubSub adapter is available now.  See: Google PubSub Adapter\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-23\nValid as Of: 2025-05-23\nVersion: 2503\n\n--- Record 784 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Document Grounding Capability - Support for Documents in TXT File Format\nDescription: The document grounding capability now supports documents in TXT file format.  See Set Up Document Grounding.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-23\nValid as Of: 2025-05-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 785 ---\nComponent: UI Theme Designer\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Theming Base Content for CF and Neo.\nDescription: The base theming content is updated to version 11.30.0. Review the changes at https://github.com/SAP/theming-base-content/releases.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-05-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 786 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Connect with SAP Cloud Application Event Hub\nDescription: You can now integrate the SAP Cloud Application Event Hub to exchange events that are distributed between the SAP cloud applications in your landscape.See Connect with SAP Cloud Application Event Hub.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-22\nValid as Of: 2025-05-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 787 ---\nComponent: SAP Build\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Store - New Content Packages\nDescription: A new set of content packages (Business and Learning contents) has been added to the store in the months of March, April, and May 2025.  Explore these content packages designed for various lines of business, such as Human Resources and SAP S/4HANA Finance.     Note  Content packages in the SAP Business Accelerator Hub display a 'New date of Publish' due to maintenance activities. However, there are no ne